      "text": "We can use the combination formula to solve this problem. The number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles from 7 is given by $\\binom{7}{3} = \\boxed{35}$.\nTo find the number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag of seven, we can use the combination formula. The combination formula is given by $\\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}$, where $n$ is the total number of items and $r$ is the number of items to be chosen. In this case, $n=7$ and $r=3$.\nSo, we have $\\binom{7}{3} = \\frac{7!}{3!(7-3)!} = \\frac{7!}{3!4!} = \\frac{7\\times6\\times5}{3\\times2\\times1} = \\boxed{35}$.\nTherefore, Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag in \\boxed{35} ways.\nThe answer is: 35",
